 "annotations": {},
 "description": "Build or mutate a node graph using maxon.GraphDescription's declarative dict syntax. Supports creating nodes (`$type`), assigning stable ids (`$id`), wiring connections via 'thisPort -> childPort' keys (the value is the nested upstream node), and setting port values inline. Example: {\"$type\":\"Output\",\"Surface -> outColor\":{\"$type\":\"Standard Material\",\"$id\":\"mat\",\"Base/Color\":[1,0,0]}}. Works for material graphs (standard/redshift) and the scene-nodes (neutron) document graph via `scope:\"document\"`. For scene-nodes, `$type` must be a node-template asset id from `list_graph_node_assets` (node_space:\"scenenodes\"), e.g. \"net.maxon.node.invert\" \u2014 NOT the net.maxon.corenode:* ids; the scene-nodes path supports creation + connections + port values (graph queries/labels are material-only). Creates the graph on demand by default.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
